{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Until when shall I entreat for you.</b> So that you recognize the great difference between the deed of the sorcerers and the divine deed, as He says 'until when,' and as He says 'only in the river they shall remain.' For indeed the deed of sorcery lasts for a limited time, and nature returns to its state immediately when the sorcery ceases, for then the constraining force upon nature is removed, as they said of blessed memory (Sanhedrin 91a): 'Why is their name כשפים? Because they contradict the heavenly host.' But the blessed El commands nature to cease, to change, and to act according to part of its force, or according to all of it, for the time that He decrees for it, and it does not defy His word."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:47.300513134Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}